# The Myth of the Sun and the Rain

In the first days, Sun and Rain lived apart. Sun held warmth in her rays, and Rain carried life-giving water in his clouds.

The world below was dying—crops withered under Sun's heat, then drowned when Rain finally came.

One day, Sun approached Rain with a proposal: "I will share my warmth gently, if you promise to return with moisture at the right time."

Rain hesitated. "How do I know you won't scorch the earth while I'm gathering my waters?"

