Rain considered. If he withheld his waters, he'd keep them safe. But the lakes were drying, and soon he'd have nothing to withhold.

He decided to trust. Rain sent mist to Sun, who multiplied it into clouds, then sent them back as gentle showers.

From this first exchange, they learned the rhythm: Sun's warmth draws water up, Rain returns it threefold to the earth, and both keep the balance that sustains all life.

But every drought and flood reminds us—this ancient partnership continues only as long as each one returns what is given, honoring the trust that makes the world bloom.
